{{also|säugen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|sūgen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|sūgan||to suck}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*sūgan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*sūganą}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*sewk-}}. The sense {{m-g|be inferior or objectionable}}, which was never common and always somewhat jocular or tongue-in-cheek, is a {{sl|de|en|suck|nocap=1}} in the same sense.

Compare {{cog|nds|sugen}}, {{cog|nl|zuigen}}, {{cog|da|suge}}.

